# Local IPOs: an industry area and a unique factory go public as companies of their own (the
# test city has a level-5 oil area and three unique factories). The area is named after the area,
# is never moved into another building when its main building is lost, and takes it back when it
# stands again. Needs a city with an industry area at level 3+ and a unique factory: the scan logs
# what it read. Their profit is fixed at ₡5,000 a week for the scenario (ipo-site-profit), whatever
# the city's week was. Nothing in the city is touched: lost buildings are only treated as lost.
name local ipos: an industry area and a unique factory list; a lost area waits and gets its home back
local-ipos on
ipo-healthy-days 1
ipo-site-profit 500000
ipo-scan
ipo-list-now area
expect-company-site area
expect-company-home same
ipo-lose-home nowhere
expect-company-home lost
ipo-home-back
expect-company-home same
expect-log has its headquarters back
ipo-list-now factory
expect-company-site factory
expect-company-home same
cleanup:
ipo-site-profit real
ipo-remove-test
local-ipos restore
